; The first pure Water spell in the game. Frost Shard was the only spell carrying the tag at all,
; and it carries Ice too - so before this, a Water build spent most of its six boon slots on Water
; boons just to reach a threshold that every other element reaches through spells. That is what the
; reachability audit could not see: it asks whether six is reachable, not what reaching it costs.
;
; A single element tag, per the element rule. What pays for the missing second tag is attunement:
; a spell whose tags are all one element scales with that element's tier instead of splitting its
; contribution, so a committed Water build gets more out of this than a dabbler does.

